/*
 * Declares the LogicalBoolOperatorValue class.
 *
 * LogicalBoolOperatorValue represents binary logical operations applied to two
 * boolean operands. These operators implement short-circuiting logical
 * semantics, meaning the right operand may not be evaluated depending on the
 * value of the left operand. The result of any logical operation is always a
 * boolean.
 *
 * Supported logical operators typically include:
 *   - logical AND  (&&),
 *   - logical OR   (||),
 *   - logical XOR  (if defined as a boolean operator in the language).
 *
 * 
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::bool_::logic
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/bool_/logic.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2022-01-17
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
